{"name":"Violet Blue","hex":"#510ac9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indigo","blocks":[{"text":"Indigo is a term used for a number of hues in the region of blue. The word comes from the ancient dye of the same name. The term \"indigo\" can refer to the color of the dye, various colors of fabric dyed with indigo dye, a spectral color, one of the seven colors of the rainbow as described by Sir Isaac Newton, or a region on the color wheel, and can include various shades of blue, ultramarine, and green-blue. Since the web era, the term has also been used for various purple and violet hues identified as \"indigo\", based on use of the term \"indigo\" in HTML web page specifications."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg/330px-Indian_indigo_dye_lump.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo"},{"title":"Majorelle Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Majorelle Blue is a clear, intense, fresh shade of deep blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Marrakech_Majorelle_Garden_2011.jpg/330px-Marrakech_Majorelle_Garden_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Majorelle_Blue"},{"title":"Violet Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Violet Blue is an American journalist, author, editor, advisor, and educator."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Violet_Blue_April_2013.jpg/330px-Violet_Blue_April_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_Blue"},{"title":"Violet Blue (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Violet Blue  is the third studio album by Japanese singer Chara, which was released on September 9, 1993. It debuted at #4 on the Japanese Oricon album charts, and charted in the top 200 for 8 weeks. It eventually sold 123,000 copies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/55/Charaioletblue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Violet_Blue_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg/500px-Passerina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APasserina_cyanea_Sam_Smith_Park_Toronto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg/500px-Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lactarius_indigo_%28Schwein.%29_Fr_939963.jpg/500px-Lactarius_indig